# Agent Instructions

`{{ .name }}` is an Intropy loader: a long-running .NET 10 worker that consumes
the `{{ .subscribes }}` message over a Dapr streaming subscription and writes
each one through its destination port.

## Project overview

- App id: `{{ .appId }}`
- Message: `{{ .subscribes }}` (the CloudEvents type the pipeline consumes)
- Topic: `{{ .channel }}`, declared in `.intropy/scaffold.json` with the
  subscription's routes; the system host renders the Dapr Subscription. The
  code names neither the pub/sub nor the topic.
- Destination port: `{{ .port }}`, declared in the system host's `Ports.cs`
- Payload type: `{{ .payloadType }}` in the sibling `../{{ .contracts }}` project
- No HTTP endpoints and no app port
- Config keys (`src/appsettings*.json`):
  - `Ports:{{ .port }}:Kind`: `Local` in Development; a deployment sets
    `Ports__{{ .port }}__Kind` (`Sftp`, `AzureBlob`)
  - `PlatformServices:IdempotencyServiceAppId`: `{{ .idempotencyAppId }}`
  - `PlatformServices:BusinessIncidentServiceAppId`: `{{ .businessIncidentsAppId }}`

## Important files

- `src/Composition/Composition.cs`: host builder, DI registrations and the
  `AddLoader` pipeline. `{{ .name }}.Composition` is both a namespace and a
  class, so nested namespaces call `Composition.Composition.CreateHostBuilder`.
- `src/Constants.cs`: component name, destination port, context keys.
- `src/Routes/{{ pascal .subscribes }}/`: the pipeline steps (`Deserializer`,
  `Validator`, `Transformer`, `Sender`) and the `Out` record.
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Unit/`: step unit tests.
- `test/{{ .name }}.Test.Integration/`: delivery, boot and composition tests
  on `Intropy.Framework.Testing` fakes (`LoaderSut` hosts them).
- `Dockerfile`: image build (`docker build --build-context contracts=../{{ .contracts }} -t {{ .appId }} .`).

## Build and test

The loader runs via its system host, which provides the pub/sub, the
destination binding and the platform services.

```bash
task build
task test        # or task test:unit / task test:integration
task coverage    # Cobertura report under the integration project's TestResults/
```

## Development notes
{{ if .empty }}
- The step bodies throw `NotImplementedException`; `task test` is red until
  they are implemented. The duplicate-ack and business-incident delivery tests
  are not scaffolded; add them with the implementation.
- Stamp the `cloudevent.subject` / `cloudevent.time` context keys from a stable
  business id and timestamp in the `Deserializer`; idempotency keys off them.
{{- else }}
- The `Deserializer` stamps `cloudevent.subject` / `cloudevent.time` from the
  order's `OrderId` / `OrderDate`; idempotency keys off them.
- The `Sender` writes `{orderId}.json` to the destination port.
{{- end }}

## Framework guidance

Framework how-to (pipelines, blocks, endpoints, Dapr components, testing) lives in the Intropy documentation at <https://docs.intropy.io>. For CLI facts, read `intropy template show` and `intropy <command> --help` at the moment you need them; template releases change.
